# Diagnostic artifacts written by golden/fixture tests ON FAILURE, for a human
# to diff against the baseline. They are outputs, never inputs, and they are
# regenerated by the next failing run — but they are untracked, so `git add -A`
# sweeps them into a commit and `git checkout --` cannot restore them. Both
# happened during the 2026-08-22 campaign.
#
# TWO patterns, because the two writers spell it differently:
#   pkg/config/compile_golden_4406_test.go  -> testdata/golden_4406.actual.json
#   userspace-dp/src/protocol/tests.rs      -> <fixture>.json.actual
#                                              (with_extension, so .json is REPLACED)
*.actual.json
*.json.actual

# Harness run output (#8302 review). newflow-ceiling-harness.sh:139 writes
# ARTIFACT_ROOT="$ROOT_DIR/artifacts/..." into the REPO ROOT, and nothing
# ignored it — so `git add -A` after a measurement run swept JSON output into
# the commit. Verified by probe: an untracked artifacts/ showed as `?? artifacts/`.
# The two pre-existing "artifacts" mentions in this file are COMMENTS, not
# patterns, which is why a grep for the word looked like coverage.
/artifacts/

# Review-process working files (plan drafts, raw reviewer outputs,
# follow-up bodies). These live under docs/pr/<n>/ during a review drive
# and must NEVER ship: they are superseded by the reviewed artifacts and
# by docs/log/<n>.md, and `git add -A` sweeps any untracked-but-not-ignored
# path into a commit. Shippable per-PR docs (none currently) would be
# allow-listed explicitly rather than read off this directory.
docs/pr/
